## 4. Database / back-end reference

Map each user action or system trigger to the data change it should cause, which variants it applies to, and the query to check it.

| Section | Action / trigger | Applies to | Expected data change | Verification query |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `[Watch / view content]` | `[On video completion]` | ✔︎ V1 ✔︎ V2 ✘ V3 | Progress record created with `content_type = 1` | `SELECT * FROM [progress_table] WHERE user_id = :uid AND item_id = :itemId AND content_type = 1;` |
| `[Read section]` | `[On panel expand]` | ✔︎ V1 ✔︎ V2 ✔︎ V3 | Progress record created with `content_type = 2` | `SELECT … ;` |
| `[Submit form, no approval]` | `[On Submit]` | ✘ V1 ✔︎ V2 ✘ V3 | Progress record created | `SELECT … ;` |
| `[Submit form, with approval]` | `[On Submit]` | ✔︎ V1 ✘ V2 ✘ V3 | Submission saved with `status = 0 (Pending)` | `SELECT … WHERE status = 0;` |
| `[File upload, with approval]` | `[On Submit]` | ✔︎ V1 ✘ V2 ✘ V3 | Upload record saved with hashed file name, `status = 0` | `SELECT … ;` |
| `[Quiz / assessment]` | `[On Submit]` | ✔︎ All | Answers and score summary saved | `SELECT … ;` |
| `[Assessment passed]` | `[Score ≥ passing score]` | ✔︎ All | Passer record saved with `expires_at = today + 1 year` | `SELECT … ;` |
| `[Status update]` | `[On Confirm]` | ✔︎ All | Status set to `[2]`; related slot or record updated | `SELECT … ;` |
| `[Negative check]` | `[Closing / deleting an item]` | ✔︎ All | **No record returned** | `SELECT … ;` → expect 0 rows |

> Use named parameters (`:uid`, `@date`) so the same queries can be reused across environments.

