## 7. Calculation / scoring rules matrix

Use this for features that compute scores, ratings, fees or other derived values. Test each input value, each boundary and the empty state.

**7.1 Input → raw value**

| Criterion | Input value | Raw value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `[Criterion 1, e.g., Follows instructions]` | YES / SOMETIMES / NO | `1.0` / `0.8` / `0.6` |
| `[Criterion 2, e.g., Error count]` | 0–4 / 5–9 / ≥10 | `1.5` / `1.2` / `0.9` |
| `[Criterion 3]` | 0–1 / 2 / ≥3 | `2.0` / `1.6` / `1.2` |
| `[Any criterion]` | *Empty* | `""` (blank) |

**7.2 Raw → rating → final result**

| Section | Raw formula | Rating thresholds | Final display |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `[Section 1]` | `Raw = C1 + C2 + C3 + C4` | `> 4.4 → A`, `> 3.4 → B`, `< 3.4 → C`, `0 → ""` | `A → [Very Good]`, `B → [OK]`, `C → [Practice]`; `0` if all inputs are empty |
| `[Section 2]` | `Raw = …` | … | … |

> Boundary values to test: exactly at each threshold (e.g., 4.4 and 3.4), just above and below it, all inputs at maximum, all at minimum, and all empty.

